WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.300
If we could

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.067
go back to the

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.669
picture that we just showed a second ago,

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.437
he was looking off to the distance.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.440
He looked really irritated and annoyed.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.342
It was a profile photo

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.578
that we just showed. There it is.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:13.046
I mean, Jamie Gangel,

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.280
you've been covering Donald Trump

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.582
for a long time.

00:00:15.582 --> 00:00:17.784
That is a pissed off Donald Trump.

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:18.585
Right.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:21.187
You know, this is not defiant.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:22.889
We've seen pictures

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.924
that sort of were sobering.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.092
No question.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:27.627
That is an angry

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:30.397
Donald Trump is Two things to point out

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:30.997
in addition

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:31.531
to the fact

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.334
that no one held the door open for him.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.570
We had been told that he was likely going

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.506
to stop in the hallway

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.274
and speak on his way,

00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:42.242
insisting or texting.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:44.310
It did not happen.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.845
And I have to wonder

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.248
if one of the reasons it didn't happen

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:50.950
is because he's in custody

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.353
and they would not allow it

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:55.622
to happen on the way in.

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:56.222
The other thing

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:56.756
I just wanted to

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.123
mention is

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:57.924
I spoke

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.192
to people who

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:02.595
have been in civil cases with him before.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:05.365
We see the public, Donald Trump.

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:06.766
We see what he posts.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:10.870
We see all this fighting and bravado.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:11.071
And

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.941
I am told that when he's in a courtroom

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.143
and I would think even more

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.611
so in a criminal case,

00:01:18.611 --> 00:01:20.680
that he's going to be respectful

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.382
of this judge

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.918
who not too long ago he posted

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:26.453
and he said, the judge

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.621
assigned to my witch hunt case,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.024
a case that's never been charged

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.793
before, capital letters hates me.

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:34.861
I'm guessing

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.063
we will hear a very different report.

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.165
And I'm being told by a source

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.333
in New York government

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.103
that the indictment has been unsealed,

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:44.270
although it's not live yet

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.705
on the website.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:46.806
As John Miller reported

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:47.774
several days ago,

00:01:47.774 --> 00:01:50.243
it is 34 charges against Donald Trump.

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:51.578
And I'm told that he pleaded

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:55.348
not guilty to all 34 of those charges.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.549
And now, of course,

00:01:56.549 --> 00:01:58.284
we wait to see what those charges are.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:01:59.219
Carrie Cordero.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:01:59.619
Yeah, well,

00:01:59.619 --> 00:01:59.853
I mean,

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.653
so so

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:02.755
we'll see what the actual substance

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:03.656
of these charges are

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.726
and whether they pertain to more crimes

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.695
or whether they just

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.063
are that many charges,

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.364
because that's each count

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.566
of a particular financial transaction,

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.634
like a check.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.703
But as we're waiting to see what

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:18.738
the text of that charging document

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:19.706
actually is,

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.040
as we're watching these visuals,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.209
one of the things that stands out to me

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.577
is just this dichotomy

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.147
between, on one hand, the justice system

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.284
trying to treat the former president

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.852
like any other defendant.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:34.988
So going through the normal process,

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:35.522
saying

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.490
having taken that time

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.325
where he had to be behind the scenes

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.827
and fingerprinted

00:02:40.827 --> 00:02:42.061
and processed through

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:42.996
whatever paperwork

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.864
needed to be done in New York.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.533
But the other side of the screen

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:49.202
showing the extensive security procedures

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.304
and all of the police presence

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.438
that's there

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.241
and the fact that there is not the public

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:58.144
in the seats behind the defendant

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:00.880
and this room is not open to the public,

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.116
just shows how not normal

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.918
this situation is,

00:03:04.918 --> 00:03:06.920
despite the justice system.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:09.856
Maybe trying to make this sort

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:10.390
of the way

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.992
other defendants would be treated.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.861
It's just not that way.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:17.430
This is a completely unique yeah.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:17.964
No, I mean,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:19.232
it is an interesting balance

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.934
of trying to act as though

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.435
we are all equal under the law.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:23.436
And Donald Trump will be treated

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:24.871
no differently than anybody else.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.072
While also obviously

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:27.040
he is a former president

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.708
and this has never happened before.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:29.242
Andy McCabe.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:29.943
And also,

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:30.910
you know, to be fair,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:32.612
I don't know

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.479
that a case like this

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:35.582
would be brought against Donald

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:37.450
Trump real estate developer

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:39.018
for the same alleged.

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:39.619
I mean, who knows?

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.620
Maybe it would be.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.556
But on the other hand, who knows?

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.258
It's really hard to say at this point,

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:46.926
having not seen the indictment yet.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:47.126
Right.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.928
But that's that's a decision

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:49.329
that I think

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:51.030
each one of us has to come to

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:52.899
after reading the document.

00:03:52.899 --> 00:03:54.801
The the DA's office

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:55.768
certainly maintains

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.303
that they bring this charge

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.671
of falsification of business records

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:01.107
and sometimes with the felony enhancement

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.642
on a fairly regular basis

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.977
against white collar defendants.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:06.246
But again, we

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:06.746
don't know

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.047
what's going to be in this

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:08.748
in this document.

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:09.649
I will say, though, Jake,

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.351
that these photographs

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:14.254
of the former president are so striking.

00:04:14.487 --> 00:04:18.057
But to me, they are very familiar

00:04:18.057 --> 00:04:21.661
in a way over a course of over 20 years.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:23.563
And the FBI, having been

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.331
with numerous people

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.533
on arrest and arraignment day.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.069
There is an undeniable

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.372
humility and humanity

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:33.973
that comes out against

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.808
whoever has been called

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.110
before the court and accused

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.946
publicly of a crime in this process.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:40.680
Whether you're

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.014
you know,

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.815
I've seen it from street level criminals

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:45.018
all the way up to CEOs and white collar

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.854
people accused of white collar offenses.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:48.655
This moment

00:04:48.655 --> 00:04:50.623
you may be sitting next to your lawyers,

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:53.259
but you are alone before a judge

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.627
and before the law

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.230
and facing some very serious allegations.

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.831
And it is a moment

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.767
that that he will never forget,

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:03.002
his family will never forget.

00:05:03.002 --> 00:05:05.238
And it's a it's a somber thing about

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.572
and he is an individual,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.207
of course, very wealthy

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.242
to the manor born

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:10.176
who has

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.210
in many ways escaped

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.680
consequences for actions

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:14.881
for decades and decades.

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:15.715
So I could see why

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:16.582
sitting at that table

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:18.318
would be particularly humbling.

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.053
He probably never thought he would ever

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:20.987
have to.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:21.421
Well, of course,

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.655
we are still waiting to find out

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.557
what exactly the charges are.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.692
But just a report.

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:27.794
Repeat my reporting from before

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.229
the indictment has been unsealed.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:32.932
A source in New York government tells me.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:35.568
It is not live yet on the website,

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.203
but there are 34 charges.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.805
And I am told from this source

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:39.605
in New York government

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:40.606
that Donald Trump

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:43.376
pleaded not guilty to all 34 counts.

